{"id": "EUVD-2026-59424", "enisaUuid": "fcbd0ce8-27a5-3753-b17c-6ea0143a3808", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niommu/dma-iommu: Fix wrong scatterlist length assignment in P2PDMA path\n\nIn iommu_dma_map_sg(), when handling PCI P2PDMA cases, the DMA length\nof the current scatterlist segment `s` is incorrectly assigned from the\nhead entry `sg->length` instead of the current entry `s->length`.\n\nThis typo causes all P2PDMA segments in the scatterlist to inherit the\nlength of the first segment, leading to corrupted DMA lengths for multi-\nsegment scatterlists.\n\nFix this by using `s->length` instead of `sg->length`.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:57:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:29", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6166cb1344f16dd403f2192f4bea6f6654f1ae1e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8646f00ce021e49f4f05bc1d4060a0c27b25d0e1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/db50fb87015b955a5a0c155293b2dd40d63a3b9e"], "aliases": ["GHSA-v74x-xvfc-h3j3", "CVE-2026-74277"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0789b016-3d6f-3ffb-ae2f-b31d0f13b283", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "4893e615-083e-384c-a022-954affbaa311", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "55c6e056-9ee8-3e22-a5f3-d51f7d3ce298", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a25e7962db0d79882c9d32fd2a67a02e79129c0e <6166cb1344f16dd403f2192f4bea6f6654f1ae1e"}, {"id": "66ccf09f-59da-3a3f-bb1d-a77958922f9e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a25e7962db0d79882c9d32fd2a67a02e79129c0e <db50fb87015b955a5a0c155293b2dd40d63a3b9e"}, {"id": "a922c9bd-5e4f-399c-8f42-ceddc534cb13", "product": {"name": "Linu